scope: |
  The control-direct suite landed WITH its fix and nothing ran it; 16 of its 39 tests could not
  run at all, because this package's own index.d.ts imports @scalascript/control and resolves
  it from the PACKAGE ROOT, while the harness symlinked the sibling into the FIXTURE dir.
  Supply it through TypeScript paths - the mechanism README names and tsconfig.json already
  used. NOT through a dependency entry: test/package.test.js freezes this package at zero
  local deps and refused exactly that, which is the design defending itself. Wiring goes in a
  NEW workflow: ci.yml is held live by uniml-ci-floor-tracks-the-aggregate, and smoke-ci.ssc
  has its own budget bug still OPEN (tests/BUGS.md smoke-suite-over-its-own-budget) - a 19 s
  check added to a suite that breached its cap three times is pushing on the weak spot.
  package.json is deliberately OUT of scope: it must stay unchanged.
done-so-far: paths supplied in 3 places; clean-room verified 39/39 + typecheck; gate proven
  in BOTH directions (OK with fix, FAIL 16/39 with it reverted)
next: add the js-packages workflow, then triage the 11 js-control-direct-* BUGS entries
